<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/qeqchi-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/qeqchi-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Q'eqchi' people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Q'eqchi' are a Maya people of Guatemala and Belize, centred on the department of Alta Verapaz and spreading into Izabal, the Petén and southern Belize.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/qumarkaj"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/qumarkaj.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Q'umarkaj</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Q'umarkaj, called Utatlán by the Spanish, was the capital of the K'iche' Maya kingdom in the highlands of Guatemala, near modern Santa Cruz del Quiché.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/al-qaim"><span class="enc-name">Al-Qa'im</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Al-Qa'im was an Abbasid caliph of the eleventh century whose authority was dominated first by the Shi'a Buyids.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/qabala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/qabala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Qabala</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Qabala is a town in northern Azerbaijan on the southern slopes of the Greater Caucasus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/qaboos-bin-said"><span class="enc-name">Qaboos bin Said</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Qaboos bin Said was sultan of Oman from 1970 to 2020, the longest-serving ruler in the Arab world at his death.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/qabus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/qabus.jpg" alt